        "Use the input landscape for the palette, material and shading. Draw one matte sandstone surface seen directly from above, filling the square edge to edge. Use broad painterly patches with subtle stepped shades, shallow irregular cracks and a few larger stone chips. Keep the contrast low so sprites and path markers remain easy to read. Avoid scattered single-pixel specks, evenly spaced decoration, hard lines along outer edges, highlights that look wet, perspective, objects, text, and borders."
